#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7e817a0-edcf-54ca-ba4c-ffe91af04675" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "972fe403-9a15-5d10-8f9f-f5c93eb586ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-2725" :question/problem "![](images/66/66dadc57556cccb04ea93a540f4958de45caf788b464267b2e5062bb52c6edb5.png)\n\nGiven $\\triangle{ABC}$ above, which of the diagrams represent the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}?$" :question/worked-solution "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\nThe correct diagram is shown below: \n\n![](images/1a/1a704d0dd679fa71874b7485173ae83d35892dba6018e170f83aa9e119bcc315.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114986 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a76efbd-cefd-5aa0-953e-8ab50bec7ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height Corresponding to an Extended Base"}] :question/id #uuid "2e6213d0-702f-5795-a99a-0051790c4e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2730" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $ABC$ shown below. Construct the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](images/72/72b40526cafc5d1db902ea9947a2808020dfadcf6a84238e8e3a2459ca95fe07.png)" :question/worked-solution "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](images/01/010d2c4de6c3df93112295eb2351247c2162a0d84a1f6e122fdca71dca72c168.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\n![](images/39/392d7d23590557ccce29b25cecabb276ee875f86c172ce15c845c13668939933.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115160 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a916099-a237-5612-b7f1-3679b7ff069d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "43c770ec-d353-5e9e-b44e-f06417dab2ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-9731" :question/problem "![](images/33/33700b49845ba054447ce69356324d3e421d256344149b447756cdbf0cf5a905.png)\n\nConsider $\\triangle ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overline{CH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overline{AB}.$ If $m\\angle BAC = 115^\\circ,$ calculate $m\\angle HCA.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of $180^\\circ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HAC+m∠BAC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{115}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={65}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\triangle ACH$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to $180^\\circ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{65}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{155}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7e817a0-edcf-54ca-ba4c-ffe91af04675" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b161b259-2a2c-531b-b051-34dd949dc4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16c9990277df1c1b212ff154c4951b59301ef5b7f8360f82b041e73a5a3a984b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386884} {:answer/id #uuid "e0792fd2-fe4a-5351-bd8d-d02531595632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/10e9f5a6af4d6d2b9c6392de91432b09620107d3dc645fc6ca65fdbda52f7c83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386885} {:answer/id